 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Roughly half each is typical, with one family leading the dance and the other paying for the venue. Then ask his parents to step up now, or Nicely decline the deal and go halfs on the venue. Weddings are supposed to be fun, not expensive. Not at all. Offering to split the venue would make you look like a martyr, and that's no way to live. Declining the deal with a friendly word leaves it open. Good idea. Weddings are supposed to be about love, not money.",
